@TMerlini   @mike-diamond  understood on the structural decision, and we’re ready to absorb §B.x as a section in ERC-8183. 
 The alignment is clean on our end : ERC-8183’s  complete(jobId, bytes32 reason)  maps directly onto the outcome envelope,  reason  carries the  commitmentRef  (keccak256 of the original  inputHash  committed at fund time), and the  JobCompleted  /  JobRejected  events anchor it on-chain. ERC-8265 §11 stays as reservation prose; ERC-8183 carries the field mapping and the cross-references to ERC-8263 / ERC-8274 thread URLs. 
 We’ll draft the ERC-8183 addition based on TMerlini’s revised §B.x and share it here before opening any PR. One coordination question :   @TMerlini  does  commitmentRef  == our  deliverable  field (submitted at  submit()  time), or is it a separate field computed at  complete()  time ? The binding  commitmentRef == settlement.jobs[jobId].inputHash  suggests it’s the same value as  deliverable , just want to confirm before we write it into the spec text.

